# save: 02-Sharks
# Sweep segment 02 -> 03: Hotel Onett out the side door, the street to the arcade (a Pogo Punk
# group on the way), the arcade's Pogo Punk and the doorway Shark (No: Yes Man Junior),
# Lifeup on the overworld, Frank and Frankystein Mark II in the yard (Lifeup on its first
# turn, then Auto Fight), back through the arcade, the town hall (Mayor Pirkle: Key to the
# shack, Yes), the hotel phone: Dad, Record, Continue (03-GiantStep starts there).
# Recorded in chunks with playtest/sweep/rec.py (padlog on the port, replayed on the late
# pads before each next chunk)
# The hotel side door: the original's CPU-time frame (hotel-door.play)
# Onett's streets lag in the original: overclock from the street on, and the port replays the
# pads the original read after each lag-merged frame (late-pads)
# Each door: the first emu sample is part-way into the load (skip K, 2 when the load spans 2
# samples), its fade-in starts a CPU-time frame later (lag K+20), and that FADE_IN after the
# load lag ends a logic frame later in the original (ignore: idle K+30; wall-clock noise). After
# a battle the same fade-in end (ignore: idle). Frankystein's PSI menu: the original's cursor
# move redraws the preview window over lag frames (8031-8032 merged) and the sample at 8030
# catches the focus on that window part-way (ignore: focus 8030)
